{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZShiftPhi","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_rearranged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_rearranged","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L93-L134","doc":"**The hexagon, rearranged.** If `T = A + B + C` commutes with `A, B, C` and the central\nhexagon holds, then `Φ(B, C) e^{iπ(A+C)} Φ(A, B) = e^{iπC} Φ(A, C) e^{iπA}`, where\n`e^{iπX} = eπ(−X)`. This is the shape of Mathlib's `hexagon_forward`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_mul_eπ_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_mul_eπ_neg","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L89-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_neg_mul_eπ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_neg_mul_eπ","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L85-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_central","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L50-L83","doc":"**The central hexagon.** If `T = A + B + C'` commutes with `A`, `B`, `C'`, then\n`e^{−iπA} Φ(C', A) e^{−iπC'} Φ(B, C') e^{−iπB} Φ(A, B) = e^{−iπT}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.hexagon_Φ","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L40-L48","doc":"The hexagon with the residue at infinity written through the three-point residues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.eπ_add","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L35-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.commute_eπ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.commute_eπ","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L32-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.commute_Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagonCentral.commute_Φ","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagonCentral.lean#L26-L29","doc":"`Φ(A, B)` commutes with anything commuting with `A` and `B`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}